WrapperToken::wrap
├── given contract is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given contract is not paused
    ├── when user has insufficient PT balance
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when user has insufficient PT allowance
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when previewWrap returns zero
    │   ├── when ptAmount is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
    │   └── when wrapped amount rounds down to zero
    │       └── it should revert with InvalidInput
    └── when previewWrap returns greater than zero
        ├── it should transfer PT from caller to wrapper
        ├── it should increase wrapper underlying token balance by assetAmount
        ├── it should mint previewWrap amount to caller
        ├── it should emit Wrapped
        ├── it should return previewWrap amount
        ├── given exchangeRate equals 10 ** DECIMALS
        │   └── it should mint wrapped tokens one-to-one with PT amount
        └── given exchangeRate is not 10 ** DECIMALS
            ├── given exchangeRate is greater than 10 ** DECIMALS
            │   ├── it should mint fewer wrapped tokens per PT than one-to-one
            │   └── it should emit Wrapped with rounded-down wrappedTokenAmount
            ├── given exchangeRate is less than 10 ** DECIMALS
            │   └── it should mint more wrapped tokens per PT than one-to-one
            └── when caller wraps then unwraps minted wrapped tokens at same exchangeRate
                └── it should not guarantee recovering the original ptAmount due to asymmetric rounding
